# DigitalPet — what to keep out of version control.
#
# The working tree is ~3.5 GB, but almost all of that is regenerable or
# third-party. What is worth tracking is the hand-written source and docs:
# android/app/src, pet-esp32/main, the archived firmware/ sources, and the
# handoff/design documents.

# --- build output (regenerable) ---------------------------------------------
build/
.gradle/
.cxx/
*.o
*.obj

# ESP-IDF: sdkconfig is generated from sdkconfig.defaults, which IS tracked.
# managed_components/ is fetched by the component manager; the .lock file
# tracked below pins the versions, so the fetch is reproducible.
pet-esp32/sdkconfig
pet-esp32/sdkconfig.old
pet-esp32/managed_components/
# NOTE: dependencies.lock is deliberately TRACKED — it pins exact ESP-IDF
# component versions + hashes (LVGL, the Waveshare BSP). The firmware works
# around specific LVGL behaviour, so a fresh clone must resolve the same
# versions rather than whatever is newest.

# --- vendored third-party sources (each is its own git clone) ---------------
# Not submodules on purpose — re-clone these if you need to rebuild natives.
/llama.cpp/
/whisper.cpp/
/piper/
/deps/
android/app/src/main/cpp/deps/

# --- large binaries and ML models (re-downloadable) -------------------------
*.jar
*.zip
*.tar.bz2
*.so
*.a
*.gguf
*.onnx
*.bin
# The wrapper jar must ship: without it a fresh clone cannot run ./gradlew.
# This negation was previously written un-prefixed, which silently never
# matched -- an anchored pattern is relative to this file, and the jar is
# under android/.
!android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# Nothing is bundled: all three models — the LLM, the Whisper .bin and the Piper
# voice — are fetched by the user and imported through the system picker. An
# earlier build shipped ggml-tiny.en.bin in assets, which cost ~75 MB in the APK
# AND ~75 MB unpacked, and made the ears the one faculty nobody chose.

# --- signing ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The release keystore and its passwords. Losing the .jks means never being able
# to update the app under the same Play listing again, so keep a backup that is
# not this repo — and never commit either file.
android/app/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# --- machine-local / transient ----------------------------------------------
local.properties
# tools/ is plain scripts run in place; the interpreter's bytecode cache was
# tracked once by accident and is regenerated on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
logcat.txt
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/
.claude/settings.local.json
